{
    "background_story": "Thiago had always been fascinated by the mysteries of the ocean. As a marine biologist, he spent most of his career studying the unique creatures that inhabit the deep sea. One day, while exploring a shipwreck, Thiago stumbled upon an ancient ampulla - a small flask used by sailors to carry holy water. Intrigued, he began to research the history of the ampulla and its significance in maritime culture. Thiago's findings led him to a groundbreaking discovery: the ampulla was actually a cleverly designed container that could preserve the delicate balance of seawater, allowing sailors to study and transport marine specimens. Thiago's discovery opened up new avenues for oceanic research, and he became a leading expert in the field, inspiring a new generation of marine biologists to explore the secrets of the deep.",
